age, what does \"queue\" mean?", "context": "The application places work items in a queue. Workers process these items when they have capacity. This separates receiving a request from completing its background work and helps absorb short bursts of demand.", "options": ["a collection of work items waiting to be processed", "a guarantee that all work finishes instantly", "a list of public encryption keys only", "a display setting for the mobile screen"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "Đáp án được hỗ trợ bởi đoạn văn: a collection of work items waiting to be processed"}, {"tag": "placement-v2-aws-clf-c02-d3-5-intermediate", "domain": "AWS_CLF_C02_D3", "level": "intermediate", "prompt": "Which statement best summarizes the passage?", "context": "The application places work items in a queue. Workers process these items when they have capacity. This separates receiving a request from completing its background work and helps absorb short bursts of demand.", "options": ["The passage says that no further customer decisions are needed.", "Workers process queued items according to their available capacity.", "The passage recommends ignoring changes in workload usage.", "The passage guarantees that every operational problem disappears."], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Đáp án được hỗ trợ bởi đoạn văn: Workers process queued items according to their available capacity."}, {"tag": "placement-v2-aws-clf-c02-d3-5-advanced", "domain": "AWS_CLF_C02_D3", "level": "advanced", "prompt": "Which conclusion is supported by the passage?", "context": "The application places work items in a queue. Workers process these items when they have capacity. This separates receiving a request from completing its background work and helps absorb short bursts of demand.", "options": ["The passage says that no further customer decisions are needed.", "The passage recommends ignoring changes in workload usage.", "A burst of incoming work need not force every item to be processed immediately.", "Th